Patch 04 — Per-voice stem capture in the mixer (Phase 4 experiment)

Why: the firmware mixer routes each voice to one of the two DAC pairs or
the FX bus; there is no per-voice breakout. This patch adds a passive tap:
after each voice's distribution call in mixer_calcNextSampleBlock (the
USE_TRIGGERED_PAN path the build actually compiles), a helper records the
voice's own stereo contribution — post voice DSP, post performance fader,
post pan, pre destination-sum saturation, pre FX — into
mixer_stemData[voice]. The tap writes only its own buffer; no firmware
state or output path is modified, so the main buses are bit-identical
(gate: tools/stem-gate.sh / STATUS Phase 4). The host wrapper exposes the
buffers as lxr_stem_data(); the plugin surfaces them as six extra stereo
output buses (disabled by default; see ARCHITECTURE).

